  Placement: 2
  CardStory: "*Someone knocks on the western gate, as I start to open my eyes and
    do the things that must be done when there is light.*\r\n\r\nSomeone knocks that
    isn\u2019t me.\r\n\r\n*He. I do not understand him. Not all of him, not yet.
    I, and I let him enter. I, and I and I take his word for what is going on in
    the capital.*\r\n\r\n*The man leaves after it becomes dark and light again. I
    do not understand him. But he\u2019s seen me now.*\r\n\r\n*I have seen him and
    so I\u2019ve seen I in him.*\r\n\r\n*So much more to understand, wherever I\u2019m
    going.*"
